# Default-deny build context. Only the inputs needed by `pip install .` are
# allowed; tests, workflows, docs, deployment units, local state, credentials
# and Git history never enter the build context. A new build input must be
# added here explicitly.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!ci_burst
!ci_burst/**

# Re-exclude generated bytecode inside an allowed directory (later pattern wins).
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
